GitGrok: AI-Driven Repository Intelligence & Contextual Archaeology
GitGrok is a high-performance RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) engine designed to bridge the gap between source code, historical intent (Git), and project requirements (Issues). It enables engineers to query a codebase not just for how it works, but why it evolved that way.

System Architecture
The platform implements a modular RAG pipeline optimized for local-first inference to ensure data privacy and zero-latency development.

Inference Engine: Ollama (Quantized phi3:mini for high throughput on commodity CPUs).

Vector Orchestration: Pinecone Serverless (High-dimensional semantic search with metadata filtering).

Backend: Spring Boot 3.4 (Structured via Spring AI for unified LLM abstraction).

Data Pipeline: Multi-threaded ingestion of Source Code (.java), Git History (Commits), and Issue Trackers.

Advanced Technical Features
1. Contextual Archaeology
Unlike standard code-search, GitGrok uses a Cross-Reference Prompting Strategy. It retrieves the code snippet AND the last 3 related commit messages to provide a holistic answer.

2. Optimized Local RAG Pipeline
Custom QuestionAnswerAdvisor: Implemented strict system prompt templates to eliminate model hallucinations and "echoing."

Streaming SSE Architecture: Utilizes Project Reactor (Flux<String>) to provide real-time word-by-word responses, maintaining a responsive UI under high CPU load.

Hybrid Semantic Search: Configured topK and similarityThreshold dynamically to balance precision and recall across large repositories.

Future Roadmap
Graph-RAG Integration: Moving from vector similarity to knowledge graphs (Neo4j) to map complex class dependencies.

Parallel Batch Ingestion: Implementing CompletableFuture pipelines to handle 10k+ file repositories efficiently.